    <string name="hbc_mac_label">Channel access (must match on all stations)</string>
    <string name="hbc_mac_help_link">ⓘ UV-5R / FT-65 defaults</string>
    <string name="hbc_mac_help_title">Recommended values — UV-5R / FT-65</string>
    <string name="hbc_mac_help_text">These radios\' VOX hang time is FIXED - it cannot be shortened in any menu - and both hold the transmitter keyed about 1.0-1.5 s after audio stops.\n\n- Baofeng UV-5R: the VOX menu only sets sensitivity (1-10), not delay.\n- Yaesu FT-65: VOX is ON/OFF only (Set Mode item 35, with the SSM-512B earpiece mic).\n\nRecommended settings (use the SAME values on every station):\n\n- Channel access: Ring\n- Guard ms: 1500 - covers the worst VOX tail\n- Skip ms: 1200 - covers the slow VOX attack\n- Max turn ms: 0 (automatic per modem)\n- VOX Lead ms: 250 - sacrificial tone so the VOX attack does not clip the data preamble\n- TX Dwell ms: 500\n\nCalibrating Guard: run a session, read the saved session log, and measure how long the carrier outlives each burst. Set Guard = worst measured hang + 150 ms.\n\nHardwired PTT (Digirig etc., no VOX): set TX output = USB + RTS PTT (0.25) - the plugin keys the radio over the Digirig serial RTS line - with Guard 300-500, VOX Lead 0.</string>
